short-term rentals are now officially  legal in unoccur unincorporated clark  county well this after commissioners  passed new rules to regulate them this  afternoon madison kimbrough is live in  our newsroom with all that information  on madison this is a big deal for  several areas around town yes it was a  unanimous vote by the board of  commissioners in favor of making  short-term rentals legal this is the  first time they are being made legal in  unincorporated areas of clark county  since previously companies like airbnb  and verbo were not allowed the nevada  legislature approved ab 363 last year  which required the county to adopt and  enforce an ordinance that would regulate  these rentals many homeowners over the  course of several months have attended  these meetings stating the reasons why  they want short-term rentals to be legal  while there may have been some who have  opposed to the idea stating that it  would harm their neighborhood and why  each person will be limited to one  license a limit of 10 people will be  allowed in each rental and properties  must be at least 2500 feet away from a  casino resort now also there must be at  least a thousand feet between properties  we will have all the new regulations  it's up on our website right now at  8newsnow.com  in the newsroom madison kimbrough live  local now
 

